On the raspberry Pi we see an expected increase in runtime, but no qualitative change of the scaling with $N_c$ over the tested range. Since the laptop and the Pi runs use different software stacks, their ratio is not a pure processor benchmark. The relevant result is that the complete candidate-and-certificate calculation remains feasible on Cortex-A53 based hardware.

